The president's words would enter through my left ear and\nleave through the right.%K%P
社长的话语，从我左耳朵进来右耳朵出去。%K%P
Well, if you were to summarize the situation with one\nterm...%K%P
嘛，总而言之，简单明了的说明一下这事的话就是…%K%P
Chain-Reaction Bankruptcy.%K%P
『连锁破产』%K%P
I was now listening to an explanation on the practical\ndetails of this very phenomenon.%K%P
这回事，不过感觉这样一语带过又有点太那个了，\n所以现在来接着详细说明一下吧。%K%P
...%K%P
………%K%P
Houei Commerce was a small establishment trading in office\ngoods.%K%P
这家邦永商会，是一家主要经营办公用品类商品的\n小小的代理商。%K%P
We were merely the seller, and as such, had to rely on the\nmanufacturing companies to supply us with products.%K%P
也就是说是经销商，而制造商另有别家，\n也就是说我们是他们的客户。%K%P
Our main supplier turned out to be a company known as East\nDevices.%K%P
然后，这家邦永商会，作为这样的客户之一\n平时刻意深化合作的对象，就是这家叫极东机械的制造商。%K%P
They seemed to have been struggling with a significant\ndrop in sales lately, which eventually led to their\nbankruptcy at the beginning of May.%K%P
然后，最近这家极东机械的销售额一落千丈，\n嘛，其实之前社长也听说各种各样的流言了，\n不过终于像现在这样真的束手无策还是从５月份开始的。%K%P
I was hired around the same time.%K%P
没错，从５月刚开始那阵。\n…正好就是我刚进入这家公司时。%K%P
Poor luck wouldn't even begin to describe it. It seemed\nalmost like everything I was involved with would come\ncrashing down.%K%P
走背字啊。\n我还真是让瘟神缠上了。%K%P
%LCPresident of Houei Commerce
%LC邦永商会社长
\dI'm really sorry, Kaya. You stayed with me to the very\nend, but...\d%K%P
「小夏夜，真是对不住。\n你都这样留到了最后了，结果还是没能…」%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\dUncle...\d%K%P
「伯父…」%K%P
The four employees of Houei Commerce were naturally\nfrightened once the president broke the news to them.%K%P
社长带来的这些传闻，让四名员工的心里，\n荡起了恐惧的波纹。%K%P
However, he would not abandon them.%K%P
但是为人宽厚的社长，\n并没有简简单单地抛弃他们。%K%P
Despite knowing he was digging the grave of his own\ncompany, he used his connections to find everyone new jobs\nand even paid proper retirement bonuses, guaranteeing\ntheir future.%K%P
他不想见到自己的公司的员工全跑掉，\n到处拜托亲戚和客户，让他们全都得到了再就业保障，\n最后还发下了一笔辞退金，确保了他们的生计。%K%P
