「抛弃了失业先生的人，是老师您吧？」%K%P
%LCAsami
%LC麻实
\d.........Eh?\d%K%P
「………诶？」%K%P
...%K%P
………%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dI hear you said you wanted to become a teacher and just\nleft.\d%K%P
「听说是您说想要当老师，\n单方面提出要离的？」%K%P
%LCAsami
%LC麻实
\d...Did Osamu's neighbor tell you that?\d%K%P
「…是从几位邻居那里听来的么？\n我们说的那些事」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dSo what if he did?\d%K%P
「那又怎么了？」%K%P
%LCAsami
%LC麻实
\dWeren't you the one who was angry with them for\neavesdropping?\d%K%P
「你明明还生气了，说他们偷听是不对的…」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dThat's a problem, yes, but what I've heard is a serious\nissue as far as our tenant is concerned. As a landlord, I\ncan't just let it slide.\d%K%P
「那是另一码事。\n这是我住客的问题。\n作为房东我不能置之不理」%K%P
%LCAsami
%LC麻实
\d...Last time I checked, normal landlords didn't involve\nthemselves in the private affairs of their tenants.\d%K%P
「…我倒是觉得普通的房东\n是不会干涉自己住客私生活到那种份上的」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dThe Terrace House Hinosaka is aiming to become an\napartment complex where the tenants can feel like they're\nall part of one big family!\d%K%P
「『Terrace House阳之坂』可是以\n如家般温暖（at home）为目标奋斗的！」%K%P
%LCAsami
%LC麻实
\dApartment complex...? I think yours is more of a boarding\nhouse...\d%K%P
「那与其说是公寓不如说是排房似的…」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dYou do realize that Mr. Laid-off lost everything after\nyou left, right? His wife, his job, his home, his money,\neven his hopes. A bit more and he might have turned up\ndead in a gutter, you know?\d%K%P
「自从老师你离开了他，失业先生就一直厄运连连。\n老婆、职务、住所、金钱连同希望一起消失了，\n那样下去什么时候死在路边也不奇怪，您知道吗？」%K%P
%LCAsami
%LC麻实
\dH-He told me a few things. ...Was it really that bad?\d%K%P
「我、我倒是听说了一些。\n…真凄惨到那种程度了么？」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dSo he hasn't told you the details, then. Why does he\nalways keep the important things to himself...?\d%K%P
「失业先生他果然还是什么都没说么。\n为什么要在这种地方留出余地啊」%K%P
%LCAsami
%LC麻实
\dWhere did that \dMr. Laid-off\d come from, anyway? That's\nquite a nickname.\d%K%P
「就算如此…你说的那个“失业先生”又是怎么回事？\n听上去好像很不得了啊这名字？」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dWhy don't you explain \dOsamu\d then? How come you're\nacting so familiar with a person you betrayed?\d%K%P
「那，“理”这称呼又是怎么回事？\n对于曾经抛弃了的对象还这样直呼其名？」%K%P
%LCAsami
%LC麻实
\d...And her retort goes after a completely different\npoint.\d%K%P
「…又是完全从相反方向出发的反驳啊」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dThat's because you keep trying to change the subject!\d%K%P
「还不是因为老师你老是想岔开话题啊！」%K%P
%LCAsami
%LC麻实
\dE-Even if that's the case... How are my private matters\nrelated to...\d%K%P
「就、就算如此，\n这事也…和这回要谈的事完全不沾边…」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dIt has an effect on how I'm supposed to act with my\ntenants as a landlord. Or rather... it already had an\neffect.\d%K%P
「作为房东而言，这会对我如何对待自己的住户产生影响。\n…不如说，已经影响了」%K%P
%LCAsami
%LC麻实
\d...Oh.\d%K%P
「………啊～」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dIf everything I heard is true, then I did something\nterrible to Mr. Laid-off. If that's the case, I have to\nfind a way to apologize.\d%K%P
「如果这事是真的，我就对失业先生做了很过分的事了。\n我觉得，我不跟他道歉是不行的」%K%P
%LCAsami
%LC麻实
\dThat's all right. Osamu wouldn't hold a grudge for things\nlike that.\d%K%P
「那其实没关系的。\n理他可是不会仅仅因为这点事就讨厌别人的」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dI know that myself! I'm just saying it's bothering me,\nokay?!\d%K%P
「这种事我当然相当清楚啊！\n我只是觉得我自己过意不去而已！」%K%P
%LCAsami
%LC麻实
\d...Why are you getting so upset over this?\d%K%P
「…为什么会这么生气啊？」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\d...Hahh.\d%K%P
「………（啊～）」%K%P
%LCAsami
%LC麻实
\d...\d%K%P
「………」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\d...I'm leaving.\d%K%P
「…回了」%K%P
%LCAsami
%LC麻实
\dEh? W-Wait, Ms. Hinosaka? I haven't finished!\d%K%P
「诶？等、等一下阳坂同学？\n我的话还没说完…」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dI ran outta time. I have to go deliver the evening\npapers.\d%K%P
「真的是到时间了。\n我得去送晚报了」%K%P
%LCAsami
%LC麻实
\dOh...\d%K%P
「啊…」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dAh, right...\d%K%P
「啊，说起来还有…」%K%P
