%LC店员
\dBe safe, Mistre... I-I mean, have a nice day!\d%K%P
「您、您请慢走…\n感谢惠顾～」%K%P
%LCAsami
%LC麻实
\d...\d%K%P
「………」%K%P
.........%K%P
………%K%P
......%K%P
……%K%P
...%K%P
…%K%P
%LCClerk
%LC店員
\dEek?!\d%K%P
「欸！？」%K%P
%LCAsami
%LC麻实
\dFor an ignorant brat, she sure likes to run her mouth...\d%K%P
「…明明就是个什么都不懂的孩子，\n在那跟什么都懂了似的，强横个什么啊」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dOh, is that true?! You really have it? About 1200 cm wide\nand made of oak? Yes... Yes!\d%K%P
「是、是真的吗！\n您是有的吧？\n１２００个宽，木质顶棚板…没错，没错！」%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\dYes, we had a sudden change in the person responsible.\nUm, try contacting Mr. Wakabayashi at Kojima OA Commerce.\d%K%P
「嗯，从下回开始主管就换人了…\n是儿岛ＯＡ销售公司的叫做若林的人…」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dI'll tell you his phone number, then. It's xx-xxxx-\nxxxx... Yes... Yes... That's right.\d%K%P
「那，我给您留一下联系方式吧？\n××－××××－××××…对，对，没错」%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\dYes. It's all right. They are going to guarantee the\nexact same kind of support as we did. The person\nresponsible will make a visit to your office at the start\nof next week.\d%K%P
「是的，没问题的。\n我们保证以后您能享有同等的售后支持。\n请您尽早，在周一之前与那边的负责人取得联系」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dThank you very much. I am truly grateful for you lending\na kind ear to all of my proposals and sudden changes. Have\na nice day.\d%K%P
「还请您多多关照。\n我们如此唐突的下单您能这么快受理，\n真的是感激不尽。那…我就先失礼了」%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\dThank you for your business up until now. Please direct\nall your future orders to Kojima OA Commerce.\d%K%P
「感谢您一直以来的支持。\n之后请您继续惠顾儿岛ＯＡ销售公司…那好」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dI sorted out the Kominami Inc. problem!\d%K%P
「小南兴业那边的客户，搞定了！」%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\dI introduced Nakaminato Devices to the place you told me\nabout.\d%K%P
「我这边也把中港电器的交接办完了」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dFantastic! Well then, let's go take care of the others!\d%K%P
「辛苦了！\n好～嘞，那么就赶紧弄下一家吧下一家～！」%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\d...How about a little break? You're starting to sound\nkind of weird.\d%K%P
「…稍微休息一会如何？\n感觉你情绪不太稳定啊？」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dNah, I thought we might as well keep this up till the\nend.\d%K%P
「呀啊，我倒是觉得不如就这样一口气全都解决掉比较好」%K%P
I'd been working for the last sixty-three hours straight,\nafter all. If I let myself relax, I would probably lose\nconsciousness right here and now.%K%P
不管怎么说，差不多已经连着工作有６３个小时了。\n只要稍微松一口气的话，我肯定就会一下子不省人事了。%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\dThough... don't you feel like it's a bit of a waste to\nput so much effort into something you know you won't get\nanything out of?\d%K%P
「不过…你干着不觉得空虚么？\n这样的工作」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dIt's for the sake of all the people that helped me over\nthe past few weeks. It's... meaningful enough.\d%K%P
「这也是为了至今为止照顾了我许多的各位。\n…是很重要的工作啊」%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\d...\d%K%P
「………」%K%P
I confirmed forty-seven companies that were relying on our\nmerchandise. Depending on their circumstances I marked\ntwelve as priority A, and the rest as priority B.%K%P
我这边认识的顾客有４７家公司。\n在这之中，现在与我们有着交易的１２家的优先度归为Ａ级，\n剩下的则归为B级。%K%P
I then had Ms. Amagi look up our rivals, and separated\nthem into ranks as well, depending on what merchandise\nthey dealt with, the information we had on their\nmanagement, and rumors about them.%K%P
然后，就是关于天城小姐介绍的其他同行公司，\n综合了销售范围、营业情况、各类传言等等因素，\n然后在这边也给上另一种意义上的优先度。%K%P
First we'd find a rival company that qualified as rank A,\nand after inquiring about their representative, introduced\nthem to our priority A clients.%K%P
首先联系上Ａ级的同行公司，\n跟他们的负责人接洽，把等级Ａ的顾客按顺序『介绍』给他们。%K%P
Both providers and clients that we marked as A were easy\nto deal with, so the negotiations for that part went\nsmoothly.%K%P
基本上来说Ａ级的都是些干得不错的代理商和客户，\n所以绝大多数都能『配对』成功。%K%P
As for priority B clients...%K%P
之后就是把这套再给优先度Ｂ的客户再用上一遍。%K%P
After first introducing lucrative A clients to get A\ncompanies interested, we'd then mention the ones whose\nconditions weren't as favorable, ultimately offering them\nall as a package deal.%K%P
先给对方介绍一些好客户，\n等稍微成交了一些金额，再把有其他条件的一些\n顾客一并介绍给他们，也就是所谓的捆绑方式。%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dThough I've got to admit it's not exactly pleasant to\nkeep cutting off clients who've been so friendly and\nhelped me so much till now.\d%K%P
「嘛，尽管如此，把积累下来的和客户之间的人脉关系，\n一个接一个地切断，\n确实挺让人不舒服就是了…」%K%P
It had only been two weeks, but there were still a few\npeople who nonetheless insisted that they'd prefer to keep\ndoing business with me.%K%P
尽管只有短短２个星期，\n但也跟不少客户说过『我们公司真的比较好』\n之类的话了。%K%P
And even though I had no choice but to turn them down, it\nstill left me feeling kind of depressed inside.%K%P
尽管如此，却要因为我们这边的行将解散，把合作关系清算干净什么的，\n果然是，让人高兴不起来的工作啊。%K%P
Still, it was an important and meaningful job to make sure\nthe number of people who'd find themselves in trouble\nafter our company's liquidation remained as low as\npossible.%K%P
就算这样，让会因为这家公司消失而陷入困境的人\n尽量减少，这也是一件非常重要的工作。%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\dYou really are a fool, you know that?\d%K%P
「真是、笨蛋啊」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dYou've been calling me that all the time lately.\d%K%P
「你最近还真爱说这话啊，天城小姐」%K%P
I suppose the biggest issue with this job was that in the\nend, it was solely about self-gratification.%K%P
而这工作唯一也是最大的问题…\n就是不论怎么想，我也是在自顾自地做着些自我满足的事。%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\dI mean, the more I think about it, the less sense it\nmakes. A newbie who got fired and wasn't even paid is\nstaying behind to sweep the floors of a sinking ship.\d%K%P
「因为我越是冷静下来考虑越是会得出这样的结论啊。\n…连工钱都没拿到的新人竟然\n一个人留下来收拾公司残局什么的」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dI'm sorry. If I was a little better at this job, I\nwouldn't have wasted so much of your time.\d%K%P
「抱歉了。\n因为我太没用了结果还让你来帮我」%K%P
Which was why Ms. Amagi's remarks hit me where it hurt the\nmost.%K%P
所以天城小姐的指摘，\n也以可畏的气势朝着１００分的靶心直刺过来。%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\dMe staying here isn't your fault. I'm doing this because\nit seems I, too, am quite the fool. Hmm, wait... I guess\nit is partly your fault, after all.\d%K%P
「我是因为和别人比起来也算是有点白痴才来的。\n跟新人君没什么关系。\n不，其实还是很有关的吧…？」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\d...I thought so.\d%K%P
「…你看果然还是有关系的吧」%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\d...Yup.\d%K%P
「…是有啊」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dI'm sorry.\d%K%P
「对不起」%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\dI hope you didn't think an apology would be enough to\nmake us even. You better tell me how you're planning on\nmaking things up to me. And make it fast.\d%K%P
「这可不是你道歉就能解决的问题吧？\n就让我好好听听你要怎么负起这个责任来吧？」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dEh...?\d%K%P
「诶…？」%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\d...\d%K%P
「………」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\d...\d%K%P
「………」%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\d...Haha.\d%K%P
「…呵呵」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dOh, I see! It was a joke. Aha... Ahaha... Ahahahaha...\d%K%P
「啊啊太好了！开玩笑的呗？\n啊哈、哈哈、啊哈哈哈哈…」%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\dI'll have you take responsibility, though.\d%K%P
「不过你可确确实实要负起责任来啊。在{别:bed}的方面」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dEh...?\d%K%P
「诶…？」%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\dHey, let's have a party after everything's done.\d%K%P
「呐。\n等把这些全都搞定了，要不要，来个庆功会？」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dA party...?\d%K%P
「庆功会…」%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\dYeah, I mean it's the weekend, and salary day to boot. I\nbet the town's bustling with life right about now.\d%K%P
「你想，今天既是周末，又是发薪日。\n大街上肯定也很热闹的吧？」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dYou have a very good sense of humor.\d%K%P
「…真是相当{有意思的:别搞笑了}玩笑啊」%K%P
Indeed, a certain air of freedom must've permeated the\ndowntown air tonight, with people enjoying their freshly-\nfattened wallets.%K%P
也就是说，现在的大街上充斥着周末的解放感，\n而且基本上都是些内心十分满足的人们愉悦不已。%K%P
I felt like someone without a single yen to his name --\nwho would soon go on an extended \dholiday\d of sorts --\nwould introduce a certain kind of dissonance to that\norchestra of gaiety.%K%P
而在那些人之中，即将过上每天都是周末，\n而且还断绝了生活来源的人，\n明显是不合群的。%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\dWhat's the big deal? You haven't been back home for two\ndays, so what's another day matter?\d%K%P
「也挺好的呗。\n都已经有两天没回家了吧？\n那再多一天不回去也不会有什么大不了的事吧？」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dWell, I suppose you're right... Wait, what?\d%K%P
「这倒也、是…诶？」%K%P
...Did she just say that?%K%P
…刚才她是不是说了什么\n越是想想越是觉得不得了的话…？%K%P
Or was my brain in such a state of exhaustion that I'd\nbeen interpreting things in an exaggerated fashion?%K%P
还是说，是我的大脑麻痹了，\n对一些无关紧要的事情过度反应了呢…？%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\dIt's decided, then. So c'mon, let's finish this crap\nalready.\d%K%P
「好嘞，就这么定了。\n那么就，赶紧把活儿弄完吧」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dAh, b-but... I don't know when I'll be done with my\npart.\d%K%P
「啊，但、但是…\n要几点才能弄完还是未知数啊？」%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\dIt's all right. I know a few places that are open all\nnight.\d%K%P
「没问题啦，我知道一家一直营业到早上的店」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dUm, that's not exactly what I meant...\d%K%P
「不、不是这方面的意思…」%K%P
Was she planning to stay with me until the very end?%K%P
她是想到最后的最后，\n对我的自我满足奉陪到底吗…%K%P
%LCKaya
